## What is Glóð?

Glóð is an initiative that supports Icelandic AI innovation with access to expertise, data, and computing power. It connects companies, startups, public bodies, and the research community to speed up the development and adoption of AI solutions.

Glóð supports both beginners and experienced developers of AI solutions. The aim is to lower barriers, speed up innovation, and expand the practical use of AI in Iceland by offering its services free of charge. Anyone interested is encouraged to get in touch.

Glóð is part of EuroHPC and connects Iceland to the LUMI supercomputer in Finland. The European Union partly funds it and is a partnership between Almannarómur, the University of Iceland, Reykjavík University, the Icelandic Met Office, Reykjavík Science Park (Vísindagarðar), and the Árni Magnússon Institute.

{% action href="https://glod.ai/" label="Visit website" /%}

{% cards columns=2 %}
{% card title="Vision" image="glod-framtidarsyn.png" %}
Glóð works to strengthen Iceland's AI ecosystem and connect it internationally through a direct link to European supercomputing and infrastructure, and to promote the responsible, scalable, and sustainable development of Icelandic AI solutions.
{% /card %}
{% card title="Role" image="glod-hlutverk.png" %}
Glóð accelerates the development of AI solutions in Iceland by providing access to high-performance computing (HPC) and expert support for solo innovators, startups, small and medium-sized enterprises, and public bodies.
{% /card %}
{% /cards %}

## About the team

Glóð offers expertise in AI and supercomputing, Icelandic datasets, and a shared workspace at Gróska. The team is made up of six member organizations from the language technology, university, and research communities, each taking on a service and support role.

{% cards %}
{% card title="Almannarómur" logo="almannaromur" %}
Leads project management and strategy, and handles communication and connections with EuroHPC, LUMI, and the European AI ecosystem.
{% /card %}
{% card title="Reykjavík University" logo="haskolinn-i-reykjavik.png" href="https://www.ru.is/" %}
Provides AI training, expert assistance, and technical support for developing AI solutions.
{% /card %}
{% card title="University of Iceland" logo="haskoli-islands.png" href="https://hi.is/" %}
Provides technical advice, support for high-performance computing (HPC), access to computing resources, and support for setting up HPC clusters.
{% /card %}
{% card title="Reykjavík Science Park (Vísindagarðar)" logo="visindagardar.png" href="https://www.visindagardar.is/" %}
Hosts the shared workspace and provides connections to startups, companies, and the innovation ecosystem.
{% /card %}
{% card title="Árni Magnússon Institute" logo="arnastofnun.png" href="https://arnastofnun.is/is" %}
Provides access to datasets and expertise in language technology for AI.
{% /card %}
{% card title="Icelandic Met Office" logo="vedurstofa-islands.png" href="https://vedur.is/" %}
Provides environmental and earth science data, along with expertise in high-performance computing (HPC).
{% /card %}
{% /cards %}
